WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.979
If you were a fan of SyFy's Krypton, then
it's easy to understand why you might be confused

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.120
by its cancellation.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.360
But it seems like there were some good reasons
for Syfy to pull the plug.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.340
Here's why Krypton was blown up earlier than
expected.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.820
If you judge it purely by critical reception,
Krypton's cancellation is confusing.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.700
Critics almost unanimously praised the series'
second season over its first.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.040
IGN's David Griffith called it "bigger and
bolder," and Eric Joseph from We Got This

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.830
Covered wrote that the series was, quote,
"finally finding its potential."

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.429
But the improvements didn't matter if no one
was watching it.

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:35.950
It's not that nobody watched Krypton's second
season, but the numbers dropped significantly.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:40.129
According to CinemaBlend, Krypton's series
premiere was Syfy's highest-rated debut in

00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:40.880
four years.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.460
But the numbers dropped from there.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.920
The average viewership for a season 1 episode
was close to 790,000.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:53.640
TV Series Finale reports that Krypton's second
season finale attracted only 350,000 viewers,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.420
less than half of the audience of most season
1 episodes.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.879
Critics of Krypton's first season wrote that
the series was a slog to bother following

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:05.400
and that it was characterized by both complicated
plotting and boring character arcs.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.720
So while those same critics may have been
impressed with Krypton's growth in the second

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.160
season, a disappointing first season may have
kept viewers away.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.380
The promise of more Doomsday and the appearance
of the violently vulgar Lobo and may not have

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.260
been enough to win back fans who stopped watching
during the first season of the show.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.240
Krypton takes place long before the birth
of Kal-El known on Earth as Superman.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:33.900
"Kal-El. My future grandson. This is the story of the house  of El."

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:39.560
The protagonist, Seg-El, is Kal's grandfather,
and when the series opens, his son Jor-El,

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.440
Superman's father, hasn't been born yet.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.490
It's a Superman show with no Superman, and
no Kryptonian even has super powers.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:49.470
You could argue that Gotham was similarly
a Batman show without Batman, but at least

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:50.600
Bruce Wayne is there.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.640
As early as the first season, it was clear
viewers were watching his evolution into the

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:55.440
Dark Knight.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.020
On Krypton, Superman hasn't even been conceived.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.280
As of its final episode, Superman's father
is an infant.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.720
Gotham took advantage of one of the Batman
franchise's chief strengths: his deep rogues'

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:06.520
gallery.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.820
Superman, on the other hand, doesn't enjoy
a wealth of popular villains.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:14.200
The most famous is Lex Luthor, and Krypton's
setting and time period make his involvement

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.380
all but impossible.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:19.980
By the end of Krypton's second season, we've
met General Zod, Brainiac, and Doomsday, and

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.960
that's pretty much it as far as popular, non-human
Superman villains are concerned.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.060
"Kneel before Zod!"

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.300
Mister Mxyzptlk might have been a possibility,
and the newly introduced villain Rogol Zaar,

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.700
who was revealed to be responsible for Krypton's
destruction in the comics, could have shown

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:36.460
up.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:40.400
Perhaps the show could have brought in Darkseid,
who's hinted at in the season 2 finale.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.940
But after that, the well's pretty dry for
space-based Superman baddies.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:48.000
Krypton's premise relies heavily on time travel
and it gets a little confusing.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.500
Adam Strange travels back from the present
to make sure things unfold as they should.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.380
"I come from a planet called Earth.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.220
A time centuries from now.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:56.580
And I've come here to warn you.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.100
Someone from the future is coming to destroy
Krypton."

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.020
"Okay.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:00.560
Right."

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.800
He brings Superman's cape with him, but it
disintegrates.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:07.500
By the end of the first season, the cape has
reappeared, but bears the sigil of Zod.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.760
There's also the odd relationship between
Seg, Lyta-Zod and Dru-Zod, who becomes General

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:12.540
Zod.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.620
Seg and Lyta are Zod's parents, and they never
seem to have a difficult time adjusting to

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:17.680
this new information.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.860
They immediately start speaking to Dru as
if they raised him, even though they just

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:21.700
met him.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:25.980
And it's a little jarring that Colin Salmon,
who plays Dru-Zod, is three decades older

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.720
than the actors playing his parents.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.340
Once Dru-Zod assumes leadership of the planet
in season 2, no one has a problem accepting

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:33.480
he's a time traveler.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.600
In the first season, acknowledging there might
be intelligent alien life in the universe

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:42.430
is considered heresy, yet in season 2 everyone
is fine with their leader having parents young

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:43.720
enough he could be their dad.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:47.140
Krypton isn't the first comic book series
to get axed by Syfy.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:52.860
In June 2019, the network announced that neither
Happy! nor Deadly Class, both based on creator-owned

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.360
comics, would be renewed.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.900
Krypton's demise took with it the upcoming
Lobo spinoff, too.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.940
Syfy could be getting skittish about comic-book-based
series.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.260
And it could have something to do with the
competition.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:06.650
Marvel has a wide slate of Disney+ MCU series
coming.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:10.410
Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. still has one more
season planned, Cloak &amp; Dagger and Runaways

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:13.819
have an upcoming crossover, and Hulu's Ghost
Rider is on its way.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:18.160
Amazon Prime's The Boys made a big splash,
as did Netflix's Umbrella Academy.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:22.180
And even though Swamp Thing barely got a chance
to prove itself, the DC Universe streaming

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:26.690
service had successes with the first seasons
of Titans and Doom Patrol, and there's still

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:27.980
the upcoming Stargirl.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:31.240
Then there's the CW's Arrowverse, which is
still going strong.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:35.250
Arrow is about to come to a close, but there's
still The Flash, Legends of Tomorrow, Supergirl,

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.380
Black Lightning, and the series premiere of
Batwoman.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:42.120
Most of those series will be involved in the
huge "Crisis on Infinite Earths" crossover.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:46.340
It could be that the powers that be at Syfy
are looking at the field of superhero and

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:49.760
comic book shows and thinking there's just
too much competition out there.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.980
"It's not superhero time."

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:56.260
Unless the creative team planned the series
to feature an alternative narrative to the

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:59.950
story we all know, Krypton would have ended
with the destruction of the planet and the

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.520
deaths of most of the characters.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:05.060
Even by the end of season 2, the show seemed
to be ditching the planet.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:09.380
Hoping to save Jor-El, Nyssa uses Adam's Zeta
Beam to go to the planet Rann.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.400
Brainiac and Jor-El are on their way to Earth.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.280
Seg and Lobo have formed a complicated alliance
of their own.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:18.620
So if Krypton had made it season 3, it doesn't
seem like much of the show would have taken

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:21.120
place on the title planet, at least for a
while.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:25.000
The show seemed to be expanding beyond the
boundaries of Superman's home planet, becoming

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.520
more of a showcase for DC's cosmic mythos.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:30.080
Krypton's very premise painted the series
in a corner.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:34.660
You can only explain how non-Kryptonian characters
keep showing up on the planet in so many ways.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:38.600
And if you go too far outside the original
setting, how do you reel the story back to

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.360
focus on the final cataclysm?

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.600
At least that's something Krypton's writers
won't have to figure out now.

